  "tool.commercial.formulas": "Percentage value: W = G · p / 100\nPercentage share: p = W / G · 100\nBase value: G = W / p · 100\nDiscount: R = P · p / 100, final price = P − R\nMarkup: A = cost · p / 100, selling price = cost + A\nMargin: M = (selling − cost) / selling · 100 · markup: (selling − cost) / cost · 100\nAdd VAT: gross = net · (1 + p/100)\nRemove VAT: net = gross / (1 + p/100)\nCash discount: S = B · p / 100, amount payable = B − S\nRule of three: x = b · c / a\nCompound interest: Kn = K0 · (1 + i)ⁿ\nAnnuity loan: A = K · i / (1 − (1 + i)⁻ⁿ)",
  "tool.commercial.assumptions": "Assumptions: a comma in the input is always the decimal separator; a dot before exactly three digits at the end counts as a thousands separator (1.234 = one thousand two hundred thirty-four), otherwise as a decimal point. Amounts are held in cents and rounded commercially, intermediate values carry twelve decimal places. Margin refers to the selling price, markup to the cost price — so both are reported together.",
