  "tool.datetime.note.deadline": "Rule under the German civil code: the day of the event does not count (§ 187), the period ends at the end of the corresponding day (§ 188) and if that falls on a weekend it ends on the next working day (§ 193). Public holidays are not considered.",
  "tool.datetime.note.workingDays": "Working days are Monday to Friday. Public holidays are not considered — that would need a calendar per federal state.",
  "tool.datetime.note.duration": "One entry per line: 1:30, 1.5h, 90min or 2h 15m. The total appears as hours:minutes and as decimal hours.",
  "tool.datetime.formulas": "Date arithmetic runs on the calendar, not on milliseconds: a month is added as a month, so 31 January plus one month gives 28 or 29 February. Working days: five per full week plus the remaining days. Durations: minutes summed, output as H:MM and as decimal hours.",
  "tool.datetime.assumptions": "Assumptions: all dates are calendar days without time and without a time zone. Months and years are added calendrically, not as fixed numbers of days. Working days and deadlines do not know public holidays. A deadline of zero days is refused.",
  "tool.datetime.sources": "Deadlines: §§ 187, 188 and 193 of the German civil code (start, end, Sunday and holiday rule). Calendar arithmetic: Temporal (TC39 polyfill, ISC; native in the browser, loaded on demand otherwise). Calendar week per ISO 8601. Own logic, no further dependency. Verified on 2026-10-03.",
