  "tool.calculator.formula": "Rules",
  "tool.calculator.formulaText": "Operator precedence: brackets, then power (right-associative: 2^3^2 = 512), then multiplication, then addition. The sign binds weaker than the power, so -2^2 = -4. A number before a bracket multiplies: 2(3+4) = 14.",
  "tool.calculator.formulaNumber": "Number model: fractions are computed as fractions and stay exact. In standard mode the calculator works with 64 digits of decimal precision and displays 14.",
  "tool.calculator.formulaAngle": "Angle mode: sin, cos and tan read their argument in the chosen unit, asin, acos and atan return it in that unit. The conversion runs through the unit arithmetic of mathjs, not a fixed factor.",
  "tool.calculator.formulaProgrammer": "Programmer mode: bitAnd, bitOr, bitXor, bitNot, leftShift and rightArithShift work on whole numbers. The representations show the same value in binary, octal and hexadecimal. The word size reads the value as two's complement (int for signed, uint for unsigned).",
  "tool.calculator.formulaRpn": "RPN: the input is read from left to right. Numbers go on the stack, binary operators take the two topmost values, unary keys the topmost one. The working shows the stack after every step.",
  "tool.calculator.sources": "Built on mathjs (Apache-2.0) using curated factories, see ADR 0005. Angle conversion, two's complement and word sizes are checked against the unit and bit functions of mathjs; rules and examples verified on 2026-10-03.",
