  "tool.roof.error.covering": "The covering must be between 1 and 50 pieces per square metre.",
  "tool.roof.assumptions": "Assumptions: the roof area is the footprint divided by the cosine of the pitch — this holds for mono-pitch, gable and hip roofs as long as the pitch is the same throughout. The overhang is applied all round. The rafter count applies per roof side: rounded-up eaves length divided by the rafter spacing, plus one rafter; hip and valley rafters are not included. On a hip roof the ridge height applies at the gable and the ridge length is taken as length minus width (square hip). Wall junctions, valleys, dormers and above-rafter insulation are not included.",
  "tool.roof.sources": "Formulas: pitch factor 1/cos(α), ridge height from width and tangent, rafter length from projected length and cosine — standard trigonometry, checked against independent recalculation in the tests. The pitch factor at 45° = 1.414 is the well-known check value. Rafter spacing, covering per square metre and allowance depend on the product and system and are therefore input fields, not fixed values. No trade standard and no statement about standards.",
  "tool.roof.roundNote": "Values are computed to twelve significant digits and displayed in the user’s language. Rafter count and covering are always rounded up.",
  "tool.wood.title": "Wood moisture and weight",
  "tool.wood.description": "Wood moisture from wet and oven-dry mass, oven-dry mass for a target moisture, and the weight of timber from dimensions and species — with the densities of the Bavarian State Institute of Forestry. Runs entirely in the browser.",
